                                  hi  3 E...A...... Hearing Impaired
                                  di  4 E...A...... Dialogue
                                  co  5 E...A...... Commentary
                                  em  6 E...A...... Emergency
                                  vo  7 E...A...... Voice Over
                                  ka  8 E...A...... Karaoke
    -request_sample_fmt sample_fmt sample format audio decoders should
                              prefer (default none)
    -sub_charenc string       set input text subtitles character encoding
    -sub_charenc_mode flags   set input text subtitles character encoding
                              mode (default 0)
                                values:
                                  do_nothing   .D...S.....
                                  auto         .D...S.....
                                  pre_decoder  .D...S.....
                                  ignore       .D...S.....
    -apply_cropping boolean   (default true)
    -skip_alpha boolean       Skip processing alpha (default false)
    -field_order int          Field order (from 0 to 5) (default 0)
                                values:
                                  progressive  1 ED.V.......
                                  tt           2 ED.V.......
                                  bb           3 ED.V.......
                                  tb           4 ED.V.......
                                  bt           5 ED.V.......
    -dump_separator string    set information dump field separator
    -codec_whitelist string   List of decoders that are allowed to be used
    -max_pixels int64         Maximum number of pixels (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default INT_MAX)
    -max_samples int64        Maximum number of samples (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default INT_MAX)
    -hwaccel_flags flags      (default ignore_level)
                                values:
                                  ignore_level            .D.V....... ignore
                                                          level even if the
                                                          codec level used
                                                          is unknown or
                                                          higher than the
                                                          maximum supported
                                                          level reported by
                                                          the hardware
                                                          driver
                                  allow_high_depth        .D.V....... allow
                                                          to output YUV
                                                          pixel formats with
                                                          a different chroma
                                                          sampling than
                                                          4:2:0 and/or other
                                                          than 8 bits per
                                                          component
                                  allow_profile_mismatch  .D.V.......
                                                          attempt to decode
                                                          anyway if HW
                                                          accelerated
                                                          decoder's
                                                          supported profiles
                                                          do not exactly
                                                          match the stream
                                  unsafe_output           .D.V....... allow
                                                          potentially unsafe
                                                          hwaccel frame
                                                          output that might
                                                          require special
                                                          care to process
                                                          successfully
    -extra_hw_frames int      Number of extra hardware frames to allocate
                              for the user (from -1 to INT_MAX) (default -1)
    -discard_damaged_percentage int Percentage of damaged samples to discard
                              a frame (from 0 to 100) (default 95)

Amv encoder AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -mpv_flags flags          Flags common for all mpegvideo-based encoders.
                              (default 0)
                                values:
                                  skip_rd     E..V....... RD optimal MB
                                              level residual skipping
                                  strict_gop  E..V....... Strictly enforce
                                              gop size
                                  qp_rd       E..V....... Use rate
                                              distortion optimization for qp
                                              selection
                                  cbp_rd      E..V....... use rate
                                              distortion optimization for
                                              CBP
                                  naq         E..V....... normalize adaptive
                                              quantization
                                  mv0         E..V....... always try a mb
                                              with mv=<0,0>
    -luma_elim_threshold int  single coefficient elimination threshold for
                              luminance (negative values also consider dc
                              coefficient) (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -chroma_elim_threshold int single coefficient elimination threshold for
                              chrominance (negative values also consider dc
                              coefficient) (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -quantizer_noise_shaping int (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -error_rate int           Simulate errors in the bitstream to test error
                              concealment. (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -qsquish float            how to keep quantizer between qmin and qmax (0
                              = clip, 1 = use differentiable function) (from
                              0 to 99) (default 0)
    -rc_qmod_amp float        experimental quantizer modulation (from
                              -FLT_MAX to FLT_MAX) (default 0)
    -rc_qmod_freq int         experimental quantizer modulation (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -rc_eq string             Set rate control equation. When computing the
                              expression, besides the standard functions
                              defined in the section 'Expression
                              Evaluation', the following functions are
                              available: bits2qp(bits), qp2bits(qp). Also
                              the following constants are available: iTex
                              pTex tex mv fCode iCount mcVar var isI isP isB
                              avgQP qComp avgIITex avgPITex avgPPTex
                              avgBPTex avgTex.
    -rc_init_cplx float       initial complexity for 1-pass encoding (from
                              -FLT_MAX to FLT_MAX) (default 0)
    -rc_buf_aggressivity float currently useless (from -FLT_MAX to FLT_MAX)
                              (default 1)
    -border_mask float        increase the quantizer for macroblocks close
                              to borders (from -FLT_MAX to FLT_MAX) (default
                              0)
    -lmin int                 minimum Lagrange factor (VBR) (from 0 to
                              INT_MAX) (default 236)
    -lmax int                 maximum Lagrange factor (VBR) (from 0 to
                              INT_MAX) (default 3658)
    -skip_threshold int       Frame skip threshold (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -skip_factor int          Frame skip factor (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -skip_exp int             Frame skip exponent (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -skip_cmp int             Frame skip compare function (from INT_MIN to
                              INT_MAX) (default dctmax)
                                values:
                                  sad     0 E..V....... Sum of absolute
                                          differences, fast
                                  sse     1 E..V....... Sum of squared
                                          errors
                                  satd    2 E..V....... Sum of absolute
                                          Hadamard transformed differences
                                  dct     3 E..V....... Sum of absolute DCT
                                          transformed differences
                                  psnr    4 E..V....... Sum of squared
                                          quantization errors, low quality
                                  bit     5 E..V....... Number of bits
                                          needed for the block
                                  rd      6 E..V....... Rate distortion
                                          optimal, slow
                                  zero    7 E..V....... Zero
                                  vsad    8 E..V....... Sum of absolute
                                          vertical differences
                                  vsse    9 E..V....... Sum of squared
                                          vertical differences
                                  nsse    10 E..V....... Noise preserving
                                          sum of squared differences
                                  dct264  14 E..V.......
                                  dctmax  13 E..V.......
                                  chroma  256 E..V.......
                                  msad    15 E..V....... Sum of absolute
                                          differences, median predicted
    -sc_threshold int         Scene change threshold (from INT_MIN to
                              INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -noise_reduction int      Noise reduction (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -ps int                   RTP payload size in bytes (from INT_MIN to
                              INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -huffman int              Huffman table strategy (from 0 to 1) (default
                              optimal)
                                values:
                                  default  0 E..V.......
                                  optimal  1 E..V.......
    -force_duplicated_matrix boolean Always write luma and chroma matrix for
                              mjpeg, useful for rtp streaming. (default
                              false)

(A)PNG encoder AVOptions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -dpi int                  Set image resolution (in dots per inch) (from
                              0 to 65536) (default 0)
    -dpm int                  Set image resolution (in dots per meter) (from
                              0 to 65536) (default 0)
    -pred int                 Prediction method (from 0 to 5) (default none)
                                values:
                                  none   0 E..V.......
                                  sub    1 E..V.......
                                  up     2 E..V.......
                                  avg    3 E..V.......
                                  paeth  4 E..V.......
                                  mixed  5 E..V.......

Cfhd AVOptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -quality int              set quality (from 0 to 12) (default film3+)
                              film3+ 0 E..V....... film2+ 2 E..V.......
                              film1+ 5 E..V....... high+ 7 E..V.......
                              medium+ 9 E..V....... low+ 11 E..V.......
                                values:
                                  film3    1 E..V.......
                                  film2    3 E..V.......
                                  film1.5  4 E..V.......
                                  film1    6 E..V.......
                                  high     8 E..V.......
                                  medium   10 E..V.......
                                  low      12 E..V.......

Cinepak AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -max_extra_cb_iterations int Max extra codebook recalculation passes,
                              more is better and slower (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 2)
    -skip_empty_cb boolean    Avoid wasting bytes, ignore vintage MacOS
                              decoder (default false)
    -max_strips int           Limit strips/frame, vintage compatible is
                              1..3, otherwise the more the better (from 1 to
                              32) (default 3)
    -min_strips int           Enforce min strips/frame, more is worse and
                              faster, must be <= max_strips (from 1 to 32)
                              (default 1)
    -strip_number_adaptivity int How fast the strip number adapts, more is
                              slightly better, much slower (from 0 to 31)
                              (default 0)

Cljr encoder AVOptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -dither_type int          Dither type (from 0 to 2) (default 1)

Dnxhd AVOptions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -nitris_compat boolean    encode with Avid Nitris compatibility (default
                              false)
    -ibias int                intra quant bias (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -profile int              (from 0 to 5) (default dnxhd)
                                values:
                                  dnxhd      0 E..V.......
                                  dnxhr_444  5 E..V.......
                                  dnxhr_hqx  4 E..V.......
                                  dnxhr_hq   3 E..V.......
                                  dnxhr_sq   2 E..V.......
                                  dnxhr_lb   1 E..V.......

Dvvideo encoder AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -quant_deadzone int       Quantizer dead zone (from 0 to 1024) (default
                              7)

Exr AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -compression int          set compression type (from 0 to 3) (default
                              none)
                                values:
                                  none   0 E..V....... none
                                  rle    1 E..V....... RLE
                                  zip1   2 E..V....... ZIP1
                                  zip16  3 E..V....... ZIP16
    -format int               set pixel type (from 1 to 2) (default float)
                                values:
                                  half   1 E..V.......
                                  float  2 E..V.......
    -gamma float              set gamma (from 0.001 to FLT_MAX) (default 1)
    -layer string             Set the decoding layer (default "")
    -part int                 Set the decoding part (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -gamma float              Set the float gamma value when decoding (from
                              0.001 to FLT_MAX) (default 1)
    -apply_trc int            color transfer characteristics to apply to EXR
                              linear input (from 1 to 18) (default gamma)
                                values:
                                  bt709         1 .D.V....... BT.709
                                  gamma         2 .D.V....... gamma
                                  gamma22       4 .D.V....... BT.470 M
                                  gamma28       5 .D.V....... BT.470 BG
                                  smpte170m     6 .D.V....... SMPTE 170 M
                                  smpte240m     7 .D.V....... SMPTE 240 M
                                  linear        8 .D.V....... Linear
                                  log           9 .D.V....... Log
                                  log_sqrt      10 .D.V....... Log square
                                                root
                                  iec61966_2_4  11 .D.V....... IEC 61966-2-4
                                  bt1361        12 .D.V....... BT.1361
                                  iec61966_2_1  13 .D.V....... IEC 61966-2-1
                                  bt2020_10bit  14 .D.V....... BT.2020 - 10
                                                bit
                                  bt2020_12bit  15 .D.V....... BT.2020 - 12
                                                bit
                                  smpte2084     16 .D.V....... SMPTE ST 2084
                                  smpte428_1    17 .D.V....... SMPTE ST
                                                428-1

Ffv1 encoder AVOptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -slicecrc boolean         Protect slices with CRCs (default auto)
    -coder int                Coder type (from -2 to 2) (default rice)
                                values:
                                  rice       0 E..V....... Golomb rice
                                  range_def  -2 E..V....... Range with
                                             default table
                                  range_tab  2 E..V....... Range with custom
                                             table
                                  ac         1 E..V....... Range with custom
                                             table (the ac option exists for
                                             compatibility and is
                                             deprecated)
    -context int              Context model (from 0 to 1) (default 0)

Ffvhuff AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -non_deterministic boolean Allow multithreading for e.g. context=1 at
                              the expense of determinism (default false)
    -pred int                 Prediction method (from 0 to 2) (default left)
                                values:
                                  left    0 E..V.......
                                  plane   1 E..V.......
                                  median  2 E..V.......
    -context int              Set per-frame huffman tables (from 0 to 1)
                              (default 0)

Generic mpegvideo encoder AVOptions ────────────────────────────────────────
    -mpv_flags flags          Flags common for all mpegvideo-based encoders.
                              (default 0)
                                values:
                                  skip_rd     E..V....... RD optimal MB
                                              level residual skipping
                                  strict_gop  E..V....... Strictly enforce
                                              gop size
                                  qp_rd       E..V....... Use rate
                                              distortion optimization for qp
                                              selection
                                  cbp_rd      E..V....... use rate
                                              distortion optimization for
                                              CBP
                                  naq         E..V....... normalize adaptive
                                              quantization
                                  mv0         E..V....... always try a mb
                                              with mv=<0,0>
    -luma_elim_threshold int  single coefficient elimination threshold for
                              luminance (negative values also consider dc
                              coefficient) (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -chroma_elim_threshold int single coefficient elimination threshold for
                              chrominance (negative values also consider dc
                              coefficient) (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -quantizer_noise_shaping int (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -error_rate int           Simulate errors in the bitstream to test error
                              concealment. (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -qsquish float            how to keep quantizer between qmin and qmax (0
                              = clip, 1 = use differentiable function) (from
                              0 to 99) (default 0)
    -rc_qmod_amp float        experimental quantizer modulation (from
                              -FLT_MAX to FLT_MAX) (default 0)
    -rc_qmod_freq int         experimental quantizer modulation (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -rc_eq string             Set rate control equation. When computing the
                              expression, besides the standard functions
                              defined in the section 'Expression
                              Evaluation', the following functions are
                              available: bits2qp(bits), qp2bits(qp). Also
                              the following constants are available: iTex
                              pTex tex mv fCode iCount mcVar var isI isP isB
                              avgQP qComp avgIITex avgPITex avgPPTex
                              avgBPTex avgTex.
    -rc_init_cplx float       initial complexity for 1-pass encoding (from
                              -FLT_MAX to FLT_MAX) (default 0)
    -rc_buf_aggressivity float currently useless (from -FLT_MAX to FLT_MAX)
                              (default 1)
    -border_mask float        increase the quantizer for macroblocks close
                              to borders (from -FLT_MAX to FLT_MAX) (default
                              0)
    -lmin int                 minimum Lagrange factor (VBR) (from 0 to
                              INT_MAX) (default 236)
    -lmax int                 maximum Lagrange factor (VBR) (from 0 to
                              INT_MAX) (default 3658)
    -skip_threshold int       Frame skip threshold (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -skip_factor int          Frame skip factor (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -skip_exp int             Frame skip exponent (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -skip_cmp int             Frame skip compare function (from INT_MIN to
                              INT_MAX) (default dctmax)
                                values:
                                  sad     0 E..V....... Sum of absolute
                                          differences, fast
                                  sse     1 E..V....... Sum of squared
                                          errors
                                  satd    2 E..V....... Sum of absolute
                                          Hadamard transformed differences
                                  dct     3 E..V....... Sum of absolute DCT
                                          transformed differences
                                  psnr    4 E..V....... Sum of squared
                                          quantization errors, low quality
                                  bit     5 E..V....... Number of bits
                                          needed for the block
                                  rd      6 E..V....... Rate distortion
                                          optimal, slow
                                  zero    7 E..V....... Zero
                                  vsad    8 E..V....... Sum of absolute
                                          vertical differences
                                  vsse    9 E..V....... Sum of squared
                                          vertical differences
                                  nsse    10 E..V....... Noise preserving
                                          sum of squared differences
                                  dct264  14 E..V.......
                                  dctmax  13 E..V.......
                                  chroma  256 E..V.......
                                  msad    15 E..V....... Sum of absolute
                                          differences, median predicted
    -sc_threshold int         Scene change threshold (from INT_MIN to
                              INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -noise_reduction int      Noise reduction (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -ps int                   RTP payload size in bytes (from INT_MIN to
                              INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -motion_est int           motion estimation algorithm (from 0 to 2)
                              (default epzs)
                                values:
                                  zero  0 E..V.......
                                  epzs  1 E..V.......
                                  xone  2 E..V.......
    -mepc int                 Motion estimation bitrate penalty compensation
                              (1.0 = 256) (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default
                              256)
    -mepre int                pre motion estimation (from INT_MIN to
                              INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -intra_penalty int        Penalty for intra blocks in block decision
                              (from 0 to 1.07374e+09) (default 0)

GIF encoder AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -gifflags flags           set GIF flags (default offsetting+transdiff)
                                values:
                                  offsetting  E..V....... enable picture
                                              offsetting
                                  transdiff   E..V....... enable
                                              transparency detection between
                                              frames
    -gifimage boolean         enable encoding only images per frame (default
                              false)
    -global_palette boolean   write a palette to the global gif header where
                              feasible (default true)

