AVFormatContext AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -avioflags flags          (default 0)
                                values:
                                  direct  ED......... reduce buffering
    -probesize int64          set probing size (from 32 to I64_MAX) (default
                              5000000)
    -formatprobesize int      number of bytes to probe file format (from 0
                              to 2.14748e+09) (default 1048576)
    -packetsize int           set packet size (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default
                              0)
    -fflags flags             (default autobsf)
                                values:
                                  flush_packets   E.......... reduce the
                                                  latency by flushing out
                                                  packets immediately
                                  ignidx          .D......... ignore index
                                  genpts          .D......... generate pts
                                  nofillin        .D......... do not fill in
                                                  missing values that can be
                                                  exactly calculated
                                  noparse         .D......... disable
                                                  AVParsers, this needs
                                                  nofillin too
                                  igndts          .D......... ignore dts
                                  discardcorrupt  .D......... discard
                                                  corrupted frames
                                  sortdts         .D......... try to
                                                  interleave outputted
                                                  packets by dts
                                  fastseek        .D......... fast but
                                                  inaccurate seeks
                                  nobuffer        .D......... reduce the
                                                  latency introduced by
                                                  optional buffering
                                  bitexact        E.......... do not write
                                                  random/volatile data
                                  shortest        E.........P stop muxing
                                                  with the shortest stream
                                  autobsf         E.......... add needed
                                                  bsfs automatically
    -seek2any boolean         allow seeking to non-keyframes on demuxer
                              level when supported (default false)
    -analyzeduration int64    specify how many microseconds are analyzed to
                              probe the input (from 0 to I64_MAX) (default
                              0)
    -cryptokey binary         decryption key
    -indexmem int             max memory used for timestamp index (per
                              stream) (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 1048576)
    -rtbufsize int            max memory used for buffering real-time frames
                              (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 3041280)
    -fdebug flags             print specific debug info (default 0)
                                values:
                                  ts  ED.........
    -max_delay int            maximum muxing or demuxing delay in
                              microseconds (from -1 to INT_MAX) (default -1)
    -start_time_realtime int64 wall-clock time when stream begins (PTS==0)
                              (from I64_MIN to I64_MAX) (default I64_MIN)
    -fpsprobesize int         number of frames used to probe fps (from -1 to
                              2.14748e+09) (default -1)
    -audio_preload int        microseconds by which audio packets should be
                              interleaved earlier (from 0 to 2.14748e+09)
                              (default 0)
    -chunk_duration int       microseconds for each chunk (from 0 to
                              2.14748e+09) (default 0)
    -chunk_size int           size in bytes for each chunk (from 0 to
                              2.14748e+09) (default 0)
    -f_err_detect flags       set error detection flags (deprecated; use
                              err_detect, save via avconv) (default
                              crccheck)
                                values:
                                  crccheck    .D......... verify embedded
                                              CRCs
                                  bitstream   .D......... detect bitstream
                                              specification deviations
                                  buffer      .D......... detect improper
                                              bitstream length
                                  explode     .D......... abort decoding on
                                              minor error detection
                                  ignore_err  .D......... ignore errors
                                  careful     .D......... consider things
                                              that violate the spec, are
                                              fast to check and have not
                                              been seen in the wild as
                                              errors
                                  compliant   .D......... consider all spec
                                              non compliancies as errors
                                  aggressive  .D......... consider things
                                              that a sane encoder shouldn't
                                              do as an error
    -err_detect flags         set error detection flags (default crccheck)
                                values:
                                  crccheck    .D......... verify embedded
                                              CRCs
                                  bitstream   .D......... detect bitstream
                                              specification deviations
                                  buffer      .D......... detect improper
                                              bitstream length
                                  explode     .D......... abort decoding on
                                              minor error detection
                                  ignore_err  .D......... ignore errors
                                  careful     .D......... consider things
                                              that violate the spec, are
                                              fast to check and have not
                                              been seen in the wild as
                                              errors
                                  compliant   .D......... consider all spec
                                              non compliancies as errors
                                  aggressive  .D......... consider things
                                              that a sane encoder shouldn't
                                              do as an error
    -use_wallclock_as_timestamps boolean use wallclock as timestamps
                              (default false)
    -skip_initial_bytes int64 set number of bytes to skip before reading
                              header and frames (from 0 to I64_MAX) (default
                              0)
    -correct_ts_overflow boolean correct single timestamp overflows (default
                              true)
    -flush_packets int        enable flushing of the I/O context after each
                              packet (from -1 to 1) (default -1)
    -metadata_header_padding int set number of bytes to be written as
                              padding in a metadata header (from -1 to
                              INT_MAX) (default -1)
    -output_ts_offset duration set output timestamp offset (default 0)
    -max_interleave_delta int64 maximum buffering duration for interleaving
                              (from 0 to I64_MAX) (default 10000000)
    -f_strict int             how strictly to follow the standards
                              (deprecated; use strict, save via avconv)
                              (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default normal)
                                values:
                                  very          2 ED......... strictly
                                                conform to a older more
                                                strict version of the spec
                                                or reference software
                                  strict        1 ED......... strictly
                                                conform to all the things in
                                                the spec no matter what the
                                                consequences
                                  normal        0 ED.........
                                  unofficial    -1 ED......... allow
                                                unofficial extensions
                                  experimental  -2 ED......... allow
                                                non-standardized
                                                experimental variants
    -strict int               how strictly to follow the standards (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default normal)
                                values:
                                  very          2 ED......... strictly
                                                conform to a older more
                                                strict version of the spec
                                                or reference software
                                  strict        1 ED......... strictly
                                                conform to all the things in
                                                the spec no matter what the
                                                consequences
                                  normal        0 ED.........
                                  unofficial    -1 ED......... allow
                                                unofficial extensions
                                  experimental  -2 ED......... allow
                                                non-standardized
                                                experimental variants
    -max_ts_probe int         maximum number of packets to read while
                              waiting for the first timestamp (from 0 to
                              INT_MAX) (default 50)
    -avoid_negative_ts int    shift timestamps so they start at 0 (from -1
                              to 2) (default auto) make_non_negative 1
                              E.......... shift timestamps so they are non
                              negative
                                values:
                                  auto       -1 E.......... enabled when
                                             required by target format
                                  disabled   0 E.......... do not change
                                             timestamps
                                  make_zero  2 E.......... shift timestamps
                                             so they start at 0
    -dump_separator string    set information dump field separator (default
                              ", ")
    -codec_whitelist string   List of decoders that are allowed to be used
    -format_whitelist string  List of demuxers that are allowed to be used
    -protocol_whitelist string List of protocols that are allowed to be used
    -protocol_blacklist string List of protocols that are not allowed to be
                              used
    -max_streams int          maximum number of streams (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 1000)
    -skip_estimate_duration_from_pts boolean skip duration calculation in
                              estimate_timings_from_pts (default false)
    -max_probe_packets int    Maximum number of packets to probe a codec
                              (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 2500)

AVIOContext AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -protocol_whitelist string List of protocols that are allowed to be used

URLContext AVOptions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -protocol_whitelist string List of protocols that are allowed to be used
    -protocol_blacklist string List of protocols that are not allowed to be
                              used
    -rw_timeout int64         Timeout for IO operations (in microseconds)
                              (from 0 to I64_MAX) (default 0)

Bluray AVOptions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -playlist int             (from -1 to 99999) (default -1)
    -angle int                (from 0 to 254) (default 0)
    -chapter int              (from 1 to 65534) (default 1)

Cache AVOptions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -read_ahead_limit int     Amount in bytes that may be read ahead when
                              seeking isn't supported, -1 for unlimited
                              (from -1 to INT_MAX) (default 65536)

Crypto AVOptions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
