Icecast AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -ice_genre string         set stream genre
    -ice_name string          set stream description
    -ice_description string   set stream description
    -ice_url string           set stream website
    -ice_public boolean       set if stream is public (default false)
    -user_agent string        override User-Agent header
    -password string          set password
    -content_type string      set content-type, MUST be set if not
                              audio/mpeg
    -legacy_icecast boolean   use legacy SOURCE method, for Icecast < v2.4
                              (default false)
    -tls boolean              use a TLS connection (default false)

Pipe AVOptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -blocksize int            set I/O operation maximum block size (from 1
                              to INT_MAX) (default INT_MAX)
    -fd int                   set file descriptor (from -1 to INT_MAX)
                              (default -1)

Prompeg AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -ttl int                  Time to live (in milliseconds, multicast only)
                              (from -1 to INT_MAX) (default -1)
-l int                        FEC L (from 4 to 20) (default 5)
-d int                        FEC D (from 4 to 20) (default 5)

Rtmp AVOptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -rtmp_app string          Name of application to connect to on the RTMP
                              server
    -rtmp_buffer int          Set buffer time in milliseconds. The default
                              is 3000. (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 3000)
    -rtmp_conn string         Append arbitrary AMF data to the Connect
                              message
    -rtmp_flashver string     Version of the Flash plugin used to run the
                              SWF player.
    -rtmp_flush_interval int  Number of packets flushed in the same request
                              (RTMPT only). (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 10)
    -rtmp_enhanced_codecs string Specify the codec(s) to use in an enhanced
                              rtmp live stream
    -rtmp_live int            Specify that the media is a live stream. (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default any)
                                values:
                                  any       -2 .D......... both
                                  live      -1 .D......... live stream
                                  recorded  0 .D......... recorded stream
    -rtmp_pageurl string      URL of the web page in which the media was
                              embedded. By default no value will be sent.
    -rtmp_playpath string     Stream identifier to play or to publish
    -rtmp_subscribe string    Name of live stream to subscribe to. Defaults
                              to rtmp_playpath.
    -rtmp_swfhash binary      SHA256 hash of the decompressed SWF file (32
                              bytes).
    -rtmp_swfsize int         Size of the decompressed SWF file, required
                              for SWFVerification. (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -rtmp_swfurl string       URL of the SWF player. By default no value
                              will be sent
    -rtmp_swfverify string    URL to player swf file, compute hash/size
                              automatically.
    -rtmp_tcurl string        URL of the target stream. Defaults to
                              proto://host[:port]/app.
    -rtmp_listen int          Listen for incoming rtmp connections (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -listen int               Listen for incoming rtmp connections (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -tcp_nodelay int          Use TCP_NODELAY to disable Nagle's algorithm
                              (from 0 to 1) (default 0)
    -timeout int              Maximum timeout (in seconds) to wait for
                              incoming connections. -1 is infinite. Implies
                              -rtmp_listen 1 (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default -1)

