    -rtmp_flush_interval int  Number of packets flushed in the same request
                              (RTMPT only). (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 10)
    -rtmp_enhanced_codecs string Specify the codec(s) to use in an enhanced
                              rtmp live stream
    -rtmp_live int            Specify that the media is a live stream. (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default any)
                                values:
                                  any       -2 .D......... both
                                  live      -1 .D......... live stream
                                  recorded  0 .D......... recorded stream
    -rtmp_pageurl string      URL of the web page in which the media was
                              embedded. By default no value will be sent.
    -rtmp_playpath string     Stream identifier to play or to publish
    -rtmp_subscribe string    Name of live stream to subscribe to. Defaults
                              to rtmp_playpath.
    -rtmp_swfhash binary      SHA256 hash of the decompressed SWF file (32
                              bytes).
    -rtmp_swfsize int         Size of the decompressed SWF file, required
                              for SWFVerification. (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -rtmp_swfurl string       URL of the SWF player. By default no value
                              will be sent
    -rtmp_swfverify string    URL to player swf file, compute hash/size
                              automatically.
    -rtmp_tcurl string        URL of the target stream. Defaults to
                              proto://host[:port]/app.
    -rtmp_listen int          Listen for incoming rtmp connections (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -listen int               Listen for incoming rtmp connections (from
                              INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -tcp_nodelay int          Use TCP_NODELAY to disable Nagle's algorithm
                              (from 0 to 1) (default 0)
    -timeout int              Maximum timeout (in seconds) to wait for
                              incoming connections. -1 is infinite. Implies
                              -rtmp_listen 1 (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX)
                              (default -1)

