Dash muxer AVOptions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -adaptation_sets string   Adaptation sets. Syntax: id=0,streams=0,1,2
                              id=1,streams=3,4 and so on
    -window_size int          number of segments kept in the manifest (from
                              0 to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -extra_window_size int    number of segments kept outside of the
                              manifest before removing from disk (from 0 to
                              INT_MAX) (default 5)
    -seg_duration duration    segment duration (in seconds, fractional value
                              can be set) (default 5)
    -frag_duration duration   fragment duration (in seconds, fractional
                              value can be set) (default 0)
    -frag_type int            set type of interval for fragments (from 0 to
                              3) (default none)
                                values:
                                  none         0 E.......... one fragment
                                               per segment
                                  every_frame  1 E.......... fragment at
                                               every frame
                                  duration     2 E.......... fragment at
                                               specific time intervals
                                  pframes      3 E.......... fragment at
                                               keyframes and following
                                               P-Frame reordering (Video
                                               only, experimental)
    -remove_at_exit boolean   remove all segments when finished (default
                              false)
    -use_template boolean     Use SegmentTemplate instead of SegmentList
                              (default true)
    -use_timeline boolean     Use SegmentTimeline in SegmentTemplate
                              (default true)
    -single_file boolean      Store all segments in one file, accessed using
                              byte ranges (default false)
    -single_file_name string  DASH-templated name to be used for baseURL.
                              Implies storing all segments in one file,
                              accessed using byte ranges
    -init_seg_name string     DASH-templated name to used for the
                              initialization segment (default
                              "init-stream$RepresentationID$.$ext$")
    -media_seg_name string    DASH-templated name to used for the media
                              segments (default
                              "chunk-stream$RepresentationID$-$Number%05d$.$
                              ext$")
    -utc_timing_url string    URL of the page that will return the UTC
                              timestamp in ISO format
    -method string            set the HTTP method
    -http_user_agent string   override User-Agent field in HTTP header
    -http_persistent boolean  Use persistent HTTP connections (default
                              false)
    -hls_playlist boolean     Generate HLS playlist files(master.m3u8,
                              media_%d.m3u8) (default false)
    -hls_master_name string   HLS master playlist name (default
                              "master.m3u8")
    -streaming boolean        Enable/Disable streaming mode of output. Each
                              frame will be moof fragment (default false)
    -timeout duration         set timeout for socket I/O operations (default
                              -0.000001)
    -index_correction boolean Enable/Disable segment index correction logic
                              (default false)
    -format_options dictionary set list of options for the container format
                              (mp4/webm) used for dash
    -global_sidx boolean      Write global SIDX atom. Applicable only for
                              single file, mp4 output, non-streaming mode
                              (default false)
    -dash_segment_type int    set dash segment files type (from 0 to 2)
                              (default auto)
                                values:
                                  auto  0 E.......... select segment file
                                        format based on codec
                                  mp4   1 E.......... make segment file in
                                        ISOBMFF format
                                  webm  2 E.......... make segment file in
                                        WebM format
    -ignore_io_errors boolean Ignore IO errors during open and write. Useful
                              for long-duration runs with network output
                              (default false)
    -lhls boolean             Enable Low-latency HLS(Experimental). Adds
                              #EXT-X-PREFETCH tag with current segment's URI
                              (default false)
    -ldash boolean            Enable Low-latency dash. Constrains the value
                              of a few elements (default false)
    -master_m3u8_publish_rate int Publish master playlist every after this
                              many segment intervals (from 0 to UINT32_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -write_prft boolean       Write producer reference time element (default
                              auto)
    -mpd_profile flags        Set profiles. Elements and values used in the
                              manifest may be constrained by them (default
                              dash)
                                values:
                                  dash      E.......... MPEG-DASH ISO Base
                                            media file format live profile
                                  dvb_dash  E.......... DVB-DASH profile
    -http_opts dictionary     HTTP protocol options
    -target_latency duration  Set desired target latency for Low-latency
                              dash (default 0)
    -min_playback_rate rational Set desired minimum playback rate (from 0.5
                              to 1.5) (default 1/1)
    -max_playback_rate rational Set desired maximum playback rate (from 0.5
                              to 1.5) (default 1/1)
    -update_period int64      Set the mpd update interval (from 0 to
                              I64_MAX) (default 0)

Mov/mp4/tgp/psp/tg2/ipod/ismv/f4v muxer AVOptions ──────────────────────────
    -movflags flags           MOV muxer flags (default 0)
                                values:
                                  rtphint               E.......... Add RTP
                                                        hint tracks
                                  empty_moov            E.......... Make the
                                                        initial moov atom
                                                        empty
                                  frag_keyframe         E.......... Fragment
                                                        at video keyframes
                                  frag_every_frame      E.......... Fragment
                                                        at every frame
                                  separate_moof         E.......... Write
                                                        separate moof/mdat
                                                        atoms for each track
                                  frag_custom           E.......... Flush
                                                        fragments on caller
                                                        requests
                                  isml                  E.......... Create a
                                                        live smooth
                                                        streaming feed (for
                                                        pushing to a
                                                        publishing point)
                                  faststart             E.......... Run a
                                                        second pass to put
                                                        the index (moov
                                                        atom) at the
                                                        beginning of the
                                                        file
                                  omit_tfhd_offset      E.......... Omit the
                                                        base data offset in
                                                        tfhd atoms
                                  disable_chpl          E.......... Disable
                                                        Nero chapter atom
                                  default_base_moof     E.......... Set the
                                                        default-base-is-moof
                                                        flag in tfhd atoms
                                  dash                  E.......... Write
                                                        DASH compatible
                                                        fragmented MP4
                                  cmaf                  E.......... Write
                                                        CMAF compatible
                                                        fragmented MP4
                                  frag_discont          E.......... Signal
                                                        that the next
                                                        fragment is
                                                        discontinuous from
                                                        earlier ones
                                  delay_moov            E.......... Delay
                                                        writing the initial
                                                        moov until the first
                                                        fragment is cut, or
                                                        until the first
                                                        fragment flush
                                  global_sidx           E.......... Write a
                                                        global sidx index at
                                                        the start of the
                                                        file
                                  skip_sidx             E.......... Skip
                                                        writing of sidx atom
                                  write_colr            E.......... Write
                                                        colr atom even if
                                                        the color info is
                                                        unspecified
                                                        (Experimental, may
                                                        be renamed or
                                                        changed, do not use
                                                        from scripts)
                                  prefer_icc            E.......... If
                                                        writing colr atom
                                                        prioritise usage of
                                                        ICC profile if it
                                                        exists in stream
                                                        packet side data
                                  write_gama            E.......... Write
                                                        deprecated gama atom
                                  use_metadata_tags     E.......... Use mdta
                                                        atom for metadata.
                                  skip_trailer          E.......... Skip
                                                        writing the
                                                        mfra/tfra/mfro
                                                        trailer for
                                                        fragmented files
                                  negative_cts_offsets  E.......... Use
                                                        negative CTS offsets
                                                        (reducing the need
                                                        for edit lists)
    -moov_size int            maximum moov size so it can be placed at the
                              begin (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -rtpflags flags           RTP muxer flags (default 0)
                                values:
                                  latm        E.......... Use MP4A-LATM
                                              packetization instead of
                                              MPEG4-GENERIC for AAC
                                  rfc2190     E.......... Use RFC 2190
                                              packetization instead of RFC
                                              4629 for H.263
                                  skip_rtcp   E.......... Don't send RTCP
                                              sender reports
                                  h264_mode0  E.......... Use mode 0 for
                                              H.264 in RTP
                                  send_bye    E.......... Send RTCP BYE
                                              packets when finishing
    -skip_iods boolean        Skip writing iods atom. (default true)
    -iods_audio_profile int   iods audio profile atom. (from -1 to 255)
                              (default -1)
    -iods_video_profile int   iods video profile atom. (from -1 to 255)
                              (default -1)
    -frag_duration int        Maximum fragment duration (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -min_frag_duration int    Minimum fragment duration (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -frag_size int            Maximum fragment size (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 0)
    -ism_lookahead int        Number of lookahead entries for ISM files
                              (from 0 to 255) (default 0)
    -video_track_timescale int set timescale of all video tracks (from 0 to
                              INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -brand string             Override major brand
    -use_editlist boolean     use edit list (default auto)
    -fragment_index int       Fragment number of the next fragment (from 1
                              to INT_MAX) (default 1)
    -mov_gamma float          gamma value for gama atom (from 0 to 10)
                              (default 0)
    -frag_interleave int      Interleave samples within fragments (max
                              number of consecutive samples, lower is
                              tighter interleaving, but with more overhead)
                              (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -encryption_scheme string Configures the encryption scheme, allowed
                              values are none, cenc-aes-ctr
    -encryption_key binary    The media encryption key (hex)
    -encryption_kid binary    The media encryption key identifier (hex)
    -use_stream_ids_as_track_ids boolean use stream ids as track ids
                              (default false)
    -write_btrt boolean       force or disable writing btrt (default auto)
    -write_tmcd boolean       force or disable writing tmcd (default auto)
    -write_prft int           Write producer reference time box with
                              specified time source (from 0 to 2) (default
                              0)
                                values:
                                  wallclock  1 E..........
                                  pts        2 E..........
    -empty_hdlr_name boolean  write zero-length name string in hdlr atoms
                              within mdia and minf atoms (default false)
    -movie_timescale int      set movie timescale (from 1 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 1000)

Fifo muxer AVOptions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -fifo_format string       Target muxer
    -queue_size int           Size of fifo queue (from 1 to INT_MAX)
                              (default 60)
